.TH WEACT-CLI 1 "October 2026" "WeAct Display Tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
weact-cli, WeActCLI \- display UTF-8 text and images on verified WeAct USB displays
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B WeActCLI
/p:DEVICE [/v] [/c:COLOR] [/f:FONT:SIZE] [/s:SPEED[:u|d]] [/center]
[/qr:DATA] [/barcode:code128|ean8|ean13|code39:DATA]
[/x:X] [/y:Y] [/CLS] [/file:PATH] [/image:PATH[:MODE[:WxH]]]
[/quality:VALUE] [--scroll-stats] [--scroll-compression off|fastlz] [text] [--serial SERIAL] [--allow-unknown-occupancy]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Linux adaptation of CheshirCa's PureBasic WeActCLI. The compatibility name
WeActCLI is a symbolic link. Parameter names are case-insensitive and accept
slash or single-dash prefixes. Use /? or /h for help.
.PP
/p:N selects /dev/ttyACMN; /p:/dev/ttyACM0 and explicit by-id paths also work.
VID:PID 1a86:fe0c and exact USB Product identify FS35 or FS096; a serial filter
is optional. Unknown USB-UARTs are rejected. No fallback port scan occurs.
.PP
Input priority is /CLS, image, UTF-8 file, text arguments, redirected stdin.
Text supports literal backslash-n, wrapping, centering and font sizes 6..32.
Fontconfig resolves system fonts, falling back to DejaVu Sans.
Scrolling speed is pixels/second; u/up or d/down select one pass then clear.
SIGINT/SIGTERM stop scrolling and close the connection.
.PP
/qr:DATA renders one centered QR Code. /barcode:FORMAT:DATA renders one
centered Code 128, EAN-8, EAN-13 or basic Code 39 symbol. The QR data delimiter
preserves later colons, so URLs are accepted. Code mode is exclusive with
text, images, files, colors, fonts, coordinates and scrolling; it uses a white
background, black modules, integer scale and required quiet zones. EAN input
of 7 or 12 digits computes the final check digit; full EAN input is validated.
QR uses UTF-8 byte mode with ECI and the system libqrencode. FS096 is limited
by its 160x80 geometry; scanner support is not certified by this manual.
.PP
Text is packed once. Consecutive one-pixel positions are sent without skipping
coordinates to catch up with blocked transfers. Actual speed may be lower than
requested when the transport is slow. On the tested FS35 run, explicit FastLZ
at 20 pixels/second produced visually smooth motion at 12.486 pixels/second.
.PP
--scroll-compression off|fastlz defaults to off. FastLZ is an explicit opt-in
for FS35 scrolling text only; it is rejected for FS096, static text and images.
--scroll-stats reports requested and actual speed, overruns, bytes, FPS,
maximum step, and bounded latency percentiles/maxima. These are host timings,
not panel commit latency. A transport failure never retries uncompressed.
.PP
Image modes: 0 fit proportionally; 1 top-left original size (oversized images
are limited to screen dimensions); 2 centered, optionally resized.
Quality fast/0 uses nearest sampling, normal/1 bilinear, high/2 bicubic;
bw/bwfast uses nearest plus a threshold, bwhigh bicubic plus a threshold.
PNG, JPEG, BMP and the first GIF frame use the system GdkPixbuf decoder.
Alpha is composited over black. Dimensions are limited to 4096x4096,
encoded images to 16 MiB, text to 256 KiB and file input to 1000 lines.
Stdin acquisition has a five-second deadline and never reads an interactive tty.
.PP
/x or /y enable sparse solid-glyph overlay: only covered runs are sent,
without clearing other pixels. Unknown-background antialiasing is unavailable.
FS096 overlay assumes an already landscape display. Overlay with scrolling or
images is rejected. The full CLI supports landscape geometry only.
.PP
--allow-unknown-occupancy accepts only foreign-process permission failures,
like weactterm; busy ports, namespace failures and identity errors remain fatal.
No experimental screen readback, sensors or WCX are implemented.
The later PureBasic /model, /orientation, /brightness, /sensor and /fastlz
extensions are rejected; the documented core syntax is supported.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success or help; 1 input/render/identity/transport failure; 2 invalid arguments;
128 plus signal number when interrupted. A transport failure never reconnects.
